{"analytics_identifier":null,"base_path":"/government/publications/community-libraries-good-practice-toolkit","content_id":"2c4ba305-c0f3-4150-9961-2fa655286e5c","description":"This good practice guide, produced by the Libraries Taskforce, (with contributions from community managed libraries) is for people who are running, or considering establishing community libraries.","details":{"attachments":[{"attachment_type":"html","command_paper_number":"","hoc_paper_number":"","id":"4318070","isbn":"","title":"Community managed libraries: good practice toolkit","unique_reference":"","unnumbered_command_paper":false,"unnumbered_hoc_paper":false,"url":"/government/publications/community-libraries-good-practice-toolkit/community-libraries-good-practice-toolkit"},{"accessible":false,"alternative_format_contact_email":"enquiries@dcms.gov.uk","assets":[{"asset_manager_id":"5ab0d900ed915d29d5695069","filename":"Considering_community_libraries_diagram__1_.pdf"}],"attachment_type":"file","command_paper_number":"","content_type":"application/pdf","file_size":108432,"filename":"Considering_community_libraries_diagram__1_.pdf","hoc_paper_number":"","id":"4318071","isbn":"","number_of_pages":1,"title":"Diagram 1: Considering community libraries","unique_reference":"","unnumbered_command_paper":false,"unnumbered_hoc_paper":false,"url":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5ab0d900ed915d29d5695069/Considering_community_libraries_diagram__1_.pdf"},{"accessible":false,"alternative_format_contact_email":"enquiries@dcms.gov.uk","assets":[{"asset_manager_id":"5ab0d8a240f0b62d854a9ba7","filename":"Setting_up_a_CML__2_.pdf"}],"attachment_type":"file","command_paper_number":"","content_type":"application/pdf","file_size":118614,"filename":"Setting_up_a_CML__2_.pdf","hoc_paper_number":"","id":"4318072","isbn":"","number_of_pages":1,"title":"Diagram 2: setting up a community managed library","unique_reference":"","unnumbered_command_paper":false,"unnumbered_hoc_paper":false,"url":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5ab0d8a240f0b62d854a9ba7/Setting_up_a_CML__2_.pdf"},{"accessible":false,"alternative_format_contact_email":"enquiries@dcms.gov.uk","assets":[{"asset_manager_id":"5ab0d8d2e5274a5e1d62d85d","filename":"Successfully_operating_a_CML_diagram__3_.pdf"}],"attachment_type":"file","command_paper_number":"","content_type":"application/pdf","file_size":73788,"filename":"Successfully_operating_a_CML_diagram__3_.pdf","hoc_paper_number":"","id":"4318073","isbn":"","number_of_pages":1,"title":"Diagram 3: successfully operating a community managed library","unique_reference":"","unnumbered_command_paper":false,"unnumbered_hoc_paper":false,"url":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5ab0d8d2e5274a5e1d62d85d/Successfully_operating_a_CML_diagram__3_.pdf"}],"body":"<div class=\"govspeak\"><p>This toolkit, produced by the <a href=\"https://www.gov.uk/government/groups/libraries-taskforce\">Libraries Taskforce</a> is for:</p>\n\n<ul>\n  <li>heads of library services who are:\n    <ul>\n      <li>considering transformational projects involving increased participation of community  volunteers and organisations in delivering their library service</li>\n      <li>supporting communities considering taking over or establishing a community managed library</li>\n      <li>supporting a community managed library that is council led</li>\n    </ul>\n  </li>\n  <li>communities who are looking to establish community managed libraries</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>The Taskforce believes that the involvement of volunteers in supporting paid staff in running public libraries can be valuable in augmenting services available and ensuring close collaboration and engagement between public libraries and the community. The Taskforce does not endorse community managed libraries with no support from the local council.</p>\n\n<p>We recognise that some councils, for various reasons, are considering a range of different models for community involvement and some already have implemented them. We want to ensure that, if this path is followed, all parties involved make informed decisions: understanding the pros and cons and learning from others who have gone before, so a high quality service is provided to local people.</p>\n\n<p>The Community Managed Libraries <a href=\"https://www.gov.uk/government/collections/community-libraries-good-practice-toolkit\">collection page</a> includes case studies and a variety of <a rel=\"external\" href=\"https://gov.uk/government/publications/exemplar-documents-and-templates-for-community-managed-libraries\">templates</a> for councils \nand organisations running community libraries.</p>\n\n<div class=\"call-to-action\">\n  <p>We are always looking to improve our toolkits. Please let us know what you think by using the feedback button at the bottom of the page (or any of the case study pages). Alternatively please email <a href=\"mailto:librariestaskforce@culture.gov.uk\">librariestaskforce@culture.gov.uk</a>.</p>\n</div>\n</div>","change_history":[{"note":"Additional sample documents added","public_timestamp":"2018-06-05T15:40:32Z"},{"note":"Revised toolkit published","public_timestamp":"2018-03-20T10:40:12Z"},{"note":"Chalfont St Giles checklist and Sutton consultation case study added","public_timestamp":"2016-07-13T08:02:20Z"},{"note":"New case studies added - Harbury Village Library and Frecheville library","public_timestamp":"2016-06-17T15:49:58Z"},{"note":"Sheffield case studies added","public_timestamp":"2016-04-20T12:33:05Z"},{"note":"Gloucestershire case studies added","public_timestamp":"2016-04-01T16:40:48Z"},{"note":"First published.","public_timestamp":"2016-03-23T17:04:00Z"}],"document_type_label":"Guidance","documents":["<section data-module=\"ga4-link-tracker\" class=\"gem-c-attachment govuk-!-margin-bottom-6\">\n  <div class=\"gem-c-attachment__thumbnail govuk-!-display-none-print\">\n    <a class=\"govuk-link\" target=\"_self\" tabindex=\"-1\" aria-hidden=\"true\" data-ga4-link=\"{&quot